<title>USA: U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. wheat weekly export sales highlights -- USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA wheat export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net sales of 964,300 metric tons (MT) were three and three-quarters times the previous week and one-half above the 4-week average.  Major Increases were reported for Egypt (463,200 MT), unknown destinations (134,000 MT), Jordan (100,000 MT), and Taiwan (80,500 MT).</p>
<p>Exports of 563,400 MT were 15 percent less than the prior week, but 6 percent more than the 4-week average.</p>
<p>The primary recipients were Egypt (151,200 MT), Morocco (51,800 MT), Japan (41,200 MT), the Philippines (40,300 MT), and South Korea (35,300 MT).</p>
</text>
